(text "Lira, wired: Raspberry Pi RP2040, USB-C only (no battery), 57 keys, built-in USB sound card" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 18 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f91baa5a-5c4e-49b4-8933-043c7d3c1645"))
(text "The wireless board (branch main: nRF52840 module, Li-Po) with the radio and the battery taken out; the RP2040 follows Raspberry Pi's 'Hardware design with RP2040' (the Pico's circuit). Differences from the wireless board:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "add43f48-807f-49a2-876a-ed884f7a3e97"))
(text "1. USB only, no battery: no Ebyte E73 (nRF52840) module, no Bluetooth, no Li-Po cell, no charger (MCP73831), no power path (B5819W + SI2301), no power switch, no battery divider, no 32.768 kHz crystal, no antenna keep-out." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "10e836b4-b7c1-4e2c-b292-18b88f0f58a8"))
(text "2. Raspberry Pi RP2040 instead of the module, with the minimum circuit of Raspberry Pi's 'Hardware design with RP2040' (the Pico's): 12 MHz crystal ABM8-272-T3 (the one Raspberry Pi qualified) with 2 x 15 pF and 1k in series on XOUT; W25Q128JV QSPI flash (16 MB) with a 10k pull-up on QSPI_SS; 100 nF (0402) on IOVDD 1, 22, 42, 49, on DVDD 23 and on ADC_AVDD, USB_VDD sharing" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3f48a23f-8537-4c62-89eb-2339bb8fe97d"))
(text "   IOVDD 49's as in the design guide, IOVDD 10 / 33 sharing 1's / 42's through a tie under the package and DVDD 50 VREG_VOUT's 1 uF through the 1.1 V ring under it; 1 uF on VREG_VIN and VREG_VOUT; each within a few mm of its pin on the bottom layer; the internal regulator makes the 1.1 V core supply; TESTEN grounded." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8342dbc1-30b6-424c-bc2d-4264ebc7c287"))
(text "3. USB: hub port 3 goes to the RP2040's USB_DP / USB_DM through 27 ohm series resistors (as on the Pico and in the design guide), instead of the module's D+ / D-." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "27ddd627-cd0e-47a5-85e9-265879acb0b7"))
(text "4. Programming: the RP2040's boot ROM is a USB drive (RPI-RP2) - no bootloader to flash with an SWD probe. A blank board starts in it; BOOT (SW101, QSPI_SS to GND through 1k) held while plugging the cable enters it again; RESET (SW102) pulls RUN low. The SWD pads stay for debugging." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "584b916f-1e82-4a77-8cf4-136aca4983fb"))
(text "5. 3.3 V regulator AP2112K-3.3 (the same as the wireless board) fed straight from VBUS: 1 uF in, 1 uF + 4.7 uF out; it also supplies the USB hub (V5 and VDD33 on 3.3 V, CH334 datasheet 6.4), so nothing but the regulator, the sound card's switch and the protection sits on VBUS." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 42 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a5b630dc-6c06-4588-8cc0-8bf8c03cac71"))
(text "6. VBUS protection at the receptacle: SMF5.0A TVS and a 4.7 uF bulk capacitor damped by 1 ohm (hot-plug ringing); VBUS divider 22k / 27k + 1 nF to GPIO29 (ADC3) for the firmware." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 45 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d5c6e61d-8904-4be6-9930-3a285572771a"))
(text "7. Status LED (red, Caps Lock) on an RP2040 GPIO, through 1k, as on the wireless board." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b823e91e-920b-4cfb-ab71-4f68d2a185f2"))
(text "8. Test points: SWD (SWCLK, SWDIO, RESET, GND) in one row in front of the RP2040, 3V3 behind it, VBUS; no VBAT / VIN." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a4d54a66-c64b-4883-8144-2cd399880ec6"))
(text "9. Sound card: the supply switch U8 is on a GPIO (GPIO12) with a 100k pull-down, as on the wireless board; the headphone amplifier's EN has its own GPIO (GPIO13) through 100k, held low by 1M (the wireless board delays it with an RC from the switch). The firmware turns the sound card on when the host has configured the keyboard, the amplifier 0.2 s later, the amplifier off in" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0e75f991-c7d4-4f87-bd97-fbbdc3560484"))
(text "   USB suspend and as soon as VBUS starts to fall." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ff4df729-87c8-4e2f-ba47-2774ef3f4b2a"))
(text "USB-C (sink: 5.1k on each CC), ESD protection, VBUS TVS and damped bulk capacitor" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 62 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cd411691-6e29-40ec-aa88-24006920e689"))
