(global_label "MIC" (shape passive) (at 386.08 340.36 180) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right)) (uuid "0ef35427-c413-41f3-a3dc-6311882e5220") (property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 386.08 340.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))))
(global_label "GND" (shape passive) (at 393.7 340.36 0) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "29b497a7-55e2-4f26-ac03-a00d84a4f9d0") (property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 393.7 340.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))))
(text "Differences from the C-Media demo board:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 376 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8efb1fbf-4461-41e3-b72d-639d1dbe6c65"))
(text "1. Supply: VBUS through a TPS22919 load switch (soft start 1.3 ms, output discharge) to AUD_5V, ON from an RP2040 GPIO (on once the host has" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 379.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "953605e8-6440-495d-b959-1a8b768dd716"))
(text "   configured the keyboard): the sound card's capacitors are charged slowly. A hard switch-on would dip VBUS enough to reset the hub (CH334 datasheet" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 382.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "338e2d53-12d6-48ff-98df-a527839f255c"))
(text "   6.1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 385.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "377072ac-178a-4746-8a98-95122d9ec2c3"))
(text "2. Headphones: a TPA6132A2 DirectPath amplifier after LOL / LOR (demo board: 100 uF + 39R straight to the jack): about 0 ohm output impedance, no" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 389.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "00fbabbe-f9e5-4513-9c3c-8419ace97073"))
(text "   coupling capacitors, 0 dB gain (-6 dB with JP3 closed, for very sensitive earphones). Inputs single-ended through 1 uF (8 Hz); EN from an RP2040" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 392.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f7cffbec-45f4-475a-a91c-437ea5ccd391"))
(text "   GPIO through 100k (1M to ground): on 0.2 s after the supply, off in USB suspend (2 mA saved) and, when the cable is pulled, as soon as the firmware" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 395.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a9625c7b-da00-4928-be26-b7c83d273db6"))
(text "   sees VBUS fall, before the codec loses its supply (no click)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 399.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7447c846-76d1-47b5-9017-8033fc18af8f"))
(text "3. Microphone: bias 1.2k + 2.2k (demo board 2.2k + 8.2k, for PC microphones) for phone headsets (Android: 1.8-2.9 V through 2.2k); 1k in series before" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 402.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "08139bcc-15bf-413b-8dc9-918eeae24205"))
(text "   MICIN against the step when a plug goes in." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 405.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9dffc789-604e-4081-942a-a6a8fba9908b"))
(text "4. The demo board's two 10 nF capacitors DVDD - DREG18 and DVDD - DREG33 ('close to IC', for ESD) are fitted; each AVDD pin (29, 34) has its own 100" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 409 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "46f94c96-042f-4981-81cb-bf9a60f01967"))
(text "   nF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 412.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7022361a-56ec-4df2-ba5f-138c52ed5518"))
(text "5. The amplifier's SGND (pin 15) is grounded at the amplifier (its ground pad and a via into the top ground plane), not on a track of its own to the" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 415.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "af6ac353-2c18-45b9-bcd3-7d1dd991d773"))
(text "   jack's ground pin as TI suggests (datasheet 10.3): with both layers poured the difference is a few millivolts." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 418.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bb55f084-e958-4c59-9653-b7712c18a604"))
(text "6. The four mode jumpers are also strapped with 10k (MODE/ADSEL low, PWRSEL/MSEL high to DREG33) on top of the chip's internal pulls. D105-D107 are" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 422.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "31cc04a3-0a67-4675-bef0-cdc6abbb39e8"))
(text "   bidirectional ESD clamps (PESD5V0S1BA) on the jack's left, right and microphone contacts, between the jack and the ferrites, each with its own" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 425.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0a40bdb1-b59c-4eea-a40a-4f6de09458ce"))
(text "   ground via: a DirectPath output swings below GND, so the clamp must be bidirectional." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 428.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f9d884f1-2a5d-4397-ad74-32116817798d"))
(text "Key matrix, col2row: column -> switch -> diode (cathode on the row). Labels: (row,col) of each key." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 210 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1d195b31-40d5-4ac2-b82a-8bdc6484fdb8"))
